        "id": "example",
        "type": "worked_example",
        "provenance": "original",
        "problem": {
          "en": "If f(x) = 3x - 1 and g(x) = x squared, find (g o f)(2) and (f o g)(2)."
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": {
              "en": "f(2) = 3 x 2 - 1 = 5, so (g o f)(2) = g(5) = 25."
            },
            "why": {
              "en": "First f, then g."
            }
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "en": "g(2) = 4, so (f o g)(2) = f(4) = 3 x 4 - 1 = 11."
            },
            "why": {
              "en": "First g, then f."
            }
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "en": "25 and 11 differ, so g o f is not the same as f o g."
            },
            "why": {
              "en": "Order of composition matters."
            }
          }
        ]
